<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n17474" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fā^brĭcātio</span></b> ,
			ōnis, f.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a
				making</i>, <i>framing</i>, <i>structure</i>, <i>manner of construction</i>
			(rare but class.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">si erit tota hominis fabricatio perspecta,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic. N. D. 2, 54, 133</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">auri,</span>”
				<i>working</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg. Sirach, 32, 8</span></i>
			.—In plur.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aedificiorum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vitr. 2,
					1</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">artificis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. 9,
				2</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">non sentiunt has injurias et contumelias
					fabricationis suae dei vestri,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tert. Apol. 12</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>, of speech, <i>structure</i>, <i>skilful construction</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. de
				Or. 3, 42, 167</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
